This extension adds S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[size=4][b][color=#b6d7a8]A configuration mod merger tool is now available. The extension will present the user with a notification asking them to download the tool:[/color][/b] [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stalker2heartofchornobyl/mods/369]https://www.nexusmods.com/stalker2heartofchornobyl/mods/369[/url][/size]

[color=#b4a7d6]Add the game in the Vortex "Games" tab. You have to include the periods when searching "S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2". Or it will be near the top of the list when sorting games by "Most Recent".[/color]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]GOG[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[size=3][b][color=#ea9999]This game does not support symlinks. You must have the mod staging folder and the game on the same drive to use this extension.[/color][/b][/size]

[size=3][b][color=#f9cb9c]UE4SS LogicMod (Blueprint) Mod Authors - You MUST include a "LogicMods" folder above your .pak file in order for this extension to install the mod to the correct location. Without this, there is no way to differentiate between LogicMod paks and regular pak mods.[/color][/b][/size]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Simple Mod Merger mods with a "simple_mod_merger.exe" file install to the "Stalker2SimpleModMerger" folder.[/*]
[*]UE4SS Script-LogicMod Combo mods with both a "Content" and a "Binaries" folder install to the "Stalker2" folder.[/*]
[*]UE4SS LogicMods (Blueprint) mods with a "LogicMods" folder install to the "Stalker2\Content\Paks" folder.[/*]
[*]Herbata Mod (GameLite) mods with a "GameLite" folder install to the "Stalker2\Content" folder.[/*]
[*]UE4SS installs to the "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64" folder ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version), recognised by a "dwmapi.dll" file.[/*]
[*]UE4SS Scripts mods with a ".lua" file and a "Scripts" folder install to the "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" folder ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version).[/*]
[*]UE4SS DLL mods with a ".dll" file and a "dlls" folder install to the "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" folder ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version).[/*]
[*]Root Game Folder mods with a top-level folder such as "Stalker2", "Engine" or "Content" install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Config (LocalAppData) mods with a config file such as "engine.ini" or "game.ini" install to the game's config folder.[/*]
[*]Saves (LocalAppData) mods with a ".sav" file install to the game's save folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64" folder ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version).[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]You can download UE4SS from Nexus Mods using the button within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]UE4SS Script and DLL mods are sorted on the "UE4SS Load Order" page and UE4SS LogicMods (Blueprint) on the "LogicMods Load Order" page.[/*]
[*]Config and Save mods only work if the game, the mod staging folder and the config/save folder are all on the same drive (limitation of hardlinks). Vortex shows a notification when they are not.[/*]
[*]For upscalers, reshades, and other mods that need to be next to the game executable, please use the "Binaries (Engine Injector)" mod type. This is the fallback mod install location if no other installer is triggered.[/*]
[*]The user has the option to download and install the[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stalker2heartofchornobyl/mods/369] Simple Mod Merger[/url]﻿ tool from a notification. The tool can be run from the Dashboard tab in Vortex after installation.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Simple Mod Merger:

Recognised when the archive contains a "simple_mod_merger.exe" file.

  Installs to: "Stalker2SimpleModMerger"

========================================================================

Combo Mods (pak + UE4SS script/DLL together):

Use this layout when one download ships both game content and UE4SS mods. It is recognised by the presence of BOTH a "Content" folder and a "Binaries" folder, laid out exactly as they appear inside the game folder.

[code]
MyComboMod.zip
├── Content\
│   └── Paks\
│       └── LogicMods\
│           └── MyBlueprintMod.pak
└── Binaries\
    └── Win64\
        └── ue4ss\
            └── Mods\
                └── MyScriptMod\
                    └── Scripts\
                        └── main.lua
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Both a "Content" folder and a "Binaries" folder must be present, or this installer is skipped.
    - Mirror the real in-game folder structure below those two folders.
    - This installer is tested before the individual pak/script/DLL installers, so a matching archive is always handled as a combo.

  Installs to: "Stalker2"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including only one of "Content" or "Binaries" - the archive then falls through to a different installer.
    - Adding an extra wrapper folder between "Binaries" and "Win64".

========================================================================

Blueprint Mods (LogicMods):

Blueprint mods built against UE4SS must sit inside a folder named "LogicMods". This is the single most common packaging mistake for Unreal games.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: A blueprint ".pak" outside a "LogicMods" folder will install, but it will not work in game.[/color][/b]

[code]
MyBlueprintMod.zip
└── LogicMods\
    └── MyBlueprintMod.pak
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - The archive must contain a folder named "LogicMods" (case does not matter).
    - Everything from the "LogicMods" folder down is copied to the game, keeping its structure.
    - Extra folders above "LogicMods" are fine - the installer finds it at any depth.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Content\Paks"

  Common mistakes:
    - Putting the ".pak" at the top level of the archive with no "LogicMods" folder. Vortex then treats it as an ordinary pak mod, installs it to the wrong place, and the blueprint mod never loads.
    - Renaming the folder ("Logic_Mods", "logicmod", "BPMods") - the name must be exactly "LogicMods".

========================================================================

Herbata Mod (GameLite):

Recognised when the archive contains a "GameLite" folder.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Content"

========================================================================

UE4SS:

This installer handles the UE4SS runtime package, not individual mods. Most authors never need it - it exists so users can install UE4SS through Vortex.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "dwmapi.dll" at any level of the archive.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64" ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version)

  Common mistakes:
    - If your script mod archive happens to contain a file named "dwmapi.dll", it will be treated as a UE4SS install rather than as your mod.

========================================================================

UE4SS Script Mods (Lua):

Lua mods for UE4SS. Recognised when the archive holds both a ".lua" file and a folder named "Scripts".

[code]
MyScriptMod.zip
└── MyScriptMod\
    └── Scripts\
        └── main.lua
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - The archive must contain a ".lua" file AND a folder named "Scripts".
    - Wrap the "Scripts" folder in a folder named after your mod. That folder name becomes the mod's UE4SS name and is what gets written to the load order.
    - If you omit the wrapper folder, Vortex falls back to naming the mod after the archive file.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version)

  Common mistakes:
    - Putting "main.lua" directly in the archive root with no "Scripts" folder - the mod is not recognised as a script mod.
    - Naming the wrapper folder something generic like "Mods" - that name is what appears in the load order.

========================================================================

UE4SS DLL Mods (C++):

Compiled UE4SS mods. Recognised when the archive holds both a ".dll" file and a folder named "dlls".

[code]
MyDllMod.zip
└── MyDllMod\
    └── dlls\
        └── main.dll
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - The archive must contain a ".dll" file AND a folder named "dlls".
    - Wrap the "dlls" folder in a folder named after your mod - that name is used in the load order.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods" ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version)

  Common mistakes:
    - A bare ".dll" with no "dlls" folder is not recognised as a UE4SS DLL mod and will reach the fallback installer.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods that replace or add files inside the game installation, laid out the same way they appear in the game folder.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── Stalker2\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a top-level folder matching any of: "Stalker2", "Engine", "Content", "Binaries", "Mods", "Paks" or "Movies".
    - The matched folder and everything below it is copied into the game folder, preserving structure.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders instead of the game folders themselves adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Config tweaks are deployed to the game's config folder in your user profile, not into the game installation.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any of these filenames in the archive: "engine.ini", "game.ini", "gameusersettings.ini", "input.ini", "scalability.ini", "hardware.ini", "deviceprofiles.ini", "compat.ini", "runtimeoptions.ini", "gameplaytags.ini", "enhancedinput.ini" or "consolevariables.ini".

  Installs to: the game's config folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod - the whole archive is then treated as a config mod.

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files are deployed to the game's save folder in your user profile.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with extension ".sav".

  Installs to: the game's save folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod - the archive is then treated as a save, not a mod.

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

This is the catch-all. Any archive with no ".pak" file that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied, unchanged, into the game's binaries folder.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: "Stalker2\Binaries\Win64" ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version)

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report it as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
